AI: 
                                   Root Cause                                   

The postgres deployment in namespace shop has 0 available replicas out of 1     
desired because the pod is in CrashLoopBackOff (11 restarts).                   

Problem: The POSTGRES_PASSWORD environment variable is set but empty. PostgreSQL
requires a non-empty password value to initialize the database.                 

Logs from last 30 minutes (18 total logs):                                      

                                                                                
 Error: Database is uninitialized and superuser password is not specified.      
        You must specify POSTGRES_PASSWORD to a non-empty value for the         
        superuser.                                                              
                                                                                


                               Deployment Status                                

 • Desired replicas: 1                                                          
 • Available replicas: 0                                                        
 • Conditions: ProgressDeadlineExceeded, MinimumReplicasUnavailable             
 • Pod: postgres-594bbc787f-5nfb7 - Exit Code 1, continuously crashing          


                                      Fix                                       

Set a non-empty password for the POSTGRES_PASSWORD environment variable:        

                                                                                
 kubectl set env deployment/postgres -n shop                                    
 POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<your-secure-password>                                       
                                                                                

Or use a Secret:                                                                

                                                                                
 kubectl create secret generic postgres-secret -n shop                          
 --from-literal=POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<your-secure-password>                        
 kubectl set env deployment/postgres -n shop --from=secret/postgres-secret      
                                                                                

Alternatively, for non-production use only, allow passwordless connections (not 
recommended):                                                                   

                                                                                
 kubectl set env deployment/postgres -n shop POSTGRES_HOST_AUTH_METHOD=trust    
                                                                                
