AI: 
                                   Root Cause                                   

Pod worker-7496d4d8b-w5tpw is not ready because it's in CrashLoopBackOff (10    
restarts). The worker container exits with code 1 when it cannot reach the      
postgres database.                                                              

Worker logs:                                                                    

                                                                                
 Tue Aug 18 07:13:58 UTC 2026 worker: cannot reach postgres                     
                                                                                

The worker's health check script (nc -z -w 2 postgres 5432) fails because the   
postgres pod (postgres-594bbc787f-5nfb7) is also in CrashLoopBackOff (11        
restarts).                                                                      

Postgres failure cause: The postgres container is misconfigured —               
POSTGRES_PASSWORD environment variable is set but empty. Postgres requires a    
non-empty password value.                                                       

Postgres logs:                                                                  

                                                                                
 Error: Database is uninitialized and superuser password is not specified.      
        You must specify POSTGRES_PASSWORD to a non-empty value for the         
        superuser. For example, "-e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=password" on "docker run" 
                                                                                


                                      Fix                                       

Set a valid password for the postgres deployment:                               

                                                                                
 kubectl set env deployment/postgres POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<your-secure-password> - 
 shop                                                                           
                                                                                

Or use trust authentication (not recommended for production):                   

                                                                                
 kubectl set env deployment/postgres POSTGRES_HOST_AUTH_METHOD=trust -n shop    
                                                                                

Once postgres starts successfully, the worker pod will automatically recover.   
