AI: 
                                   Root Cause                                   

Pod api-5d46ddb744-4drng crashes because it cannot reach the postgres database  
on port 5432. The postgres pod itself is also crash looping.                    

Postgres failure: The postgres-594bbc787f-5nfb7 pod fails immediately on startup
with:                                                                           

                                                                                
 Error: Database is uninitialized and superuser password is not specified.      
 You must specify POSTGRES_PASSWORD to a non-empty value for the superuser.     
                                                                                

The postgres deployment has POSTGRES_PASSWORD set to an empty string. PostgreSQL
requires a non-empty password.                                                  

API failure cascade: The api pod runs a health check loop that attempts to      
connect to postgres:5432 using nc -z -w 2 postgres 5432. When this fails, it    
exits with code 1, triggering CrashLoopBackOff.                                 

Logs (last 20 minutes):                                                         

                                                                                
 Tue Aug 18 07:18:04 UTC 2026 api: cannot reach postgres                        
                                                                                


                                      Fix                                       

Set a valid POSTGRES_PASSWORD in the postgres deployment:                       

                                                                                
 kubectl set env deployment/postgres -n shop POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<secure-password 
                                                                                

Or use a Secret:                                                                

                                                                                
 kubectl create secret generic postgres-secret -n shop                          
 --from-literal=POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<secure-password>                             
 kubectl patch deployment postgres -n shop --type='json' -p='[{"op": "replace", 
 "path": "/spec/template/spec/containers/0/env/0/value", "op": "add", "path":   
 "/spec/template/spec/containers/0/env/0/valueFrom", "value": {"secretKeyRef":  
 {"name": "postgres-secret", "key": "POSTGRES_PASSWORD"}}}]'                    
                                                                                

Once postgres starts successfully, the api pod will connect and stop crashing.  
