AI: 
                                   Root Cause                                   

The worker deployment in shop namespace has 1 desired replica but 0 available   
replicas because the worker pod is crash-looping (11 restarts).                 

The worker pod exits with code 1 because it cannot reach the postgres database. 
Logs show:                                                                      

                                                                                
 Tue Aug 18 07:19:03 UTC 2026 worker: cannot reach postgres                     
                                                                                

The postgres dependency is failing because the postgres pod is also             
crash-looping (11 restarts) due to a missing required environment variable:     

                                                                                
 Error: Database is uninitialized and superuser password is not specified.      
 You must specify POSTGRES_PASSWORD to a non-empty value for the superuser.     
                                                                                

The postgres deployment has POSTGRES_PASSWORD set to an empty string in its     
environment configuration.                                                      


                                      Fix                                       

Set the POSTGRES_PASSWORD environment variable in the postgres deployment:      

                                                                                
 kubectl set env deployment/postgres -n shop POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<your-password>  
                                                                                

Or patch the deployment with a proper password value. Once postgres starts      
successfully, the worker pod will be able to connect and become available,      
resolving the replica mismatch.                                                 
